Needs a multi-megabyte FAT16 medium and ~100 s of wall clock (the bed's
BOT write path moves ~30 KB/s), both past the battery's budget. Run by
hand, green 2026-08-04:

  build/compile.ps1 -Src codex/test/apps/fat-write-big.codex -Out t.cdx -Log t.log -Kernel seed/Codex.cdx
  copy seed\Codex.img fwb.img  (clear read-only)
  tools/codex-vm.exe -kernel t.cdx -mem 3072 -headless -disk fwb.img -output t.out

Expected:
  disk=1 mount=1
  write=1
  size=3000000 read=3000000 bad=0

The standing automated coverage for the writer is `fat-write` (the
small-file path), `fat-write-guard` (the allocator's volume bound, the
collision guard's refusing AND admitting arms, chain rollback, and a
forced post-allocation failure that must leak nothing) and the desk
screenshot arm (F12 under codex-vm with a disk; extract SHhhmmss.BMP
from the image by FAT chain), plus this file's recipe. What only this
file reaches is SCALE: 3 MB through the multi-cluster path, where
`fat-write-guard` writes 3 KB on a 45-cluster volume.
